      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is logically where we begin using a layer only stopping system? \n\nAnd the logic is that the shading draw cannot match with its parent depth-only draw, so treating the stop layer inclusively is sufficient? \n\nAnd if we had a stencil draw affected by a depth only, it would naturally intersect and stop traversal?",
      "revId": "037860a749feb88725771661d743bf042d90f61d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1e2df0a_ac604e78",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
